    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). There's a single concrete test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and its new GOLD checkpoint is green along with everything else.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` is `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern where derived tier inputs (`namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`) are computed once at create time, persisted, and read back by the transient getter on GET.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column household_size`) with accessors, and extended `getMembershipTier()` to return `GOLD` first when `householdSize >= 3`, keeping the SILVER/BRONZE logic unchanged.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 for new owners, stamps `householdSize` via a small `householdSizeIncluding(owner)` helper: owners already sharing the `householdId` plus the owner itself (1 for an owner with no shared household). This runs after `shareHousehold` has assigned/backfilled the shared id, alongside the existing namesake/bulk stamping.\n\n3. **`OwnerRepository`** + all three implementations (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 added `countByHouseholdId(String)`, mirroring the existing `countByCity` / `countByRegistrationDate` methods.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to the owners table in all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb used by tests, plus h2/postgres/mysql for consistency).\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule (the field is an unconstrained string, so no enum change was needed).\n\nNote: the JDBC implementation's `save` only persists the base owner columns (like the other derived fields), so the JDBC profile doesn't round-trip these stamped values \u2014 this is pre-existing behavior; the active `spring-data-jpa` profile maps the new column automatically.",
